    <custom_item>
      type        : CMD_EXEC
      description : "1.12 RHEL-09-212015"
      info        : "RHEL 9 must disable the ability of systemd to spawn an interactive boot process.

GROUP ID: V-257788
RULE ID: SV-257788r1044838

Using interactive or recovery boot, the console user could disable auditing, firewalls, or other services, weakening system security."
      solution    : "Configure the current GRUB 2 configuration to disable the ability of systemd to spawn an interactive boot process with the following command:

$ sudo grubby --update-kernel=ALL --remove-args=\"systemd.confirm_spawn\""
      reference   : "800-171|3.4.2,800-171r3|03.04.02a.,800-53|CM-6b.,800-53r5|CM-6b.,CAT|II,CCI|CCI-000366,CN-L3|8.1.10.6(d),CSF|PR.IP-1,CSF2.0|DE.CM-09,CSF2.0|PR.PS-01,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ISO-27001-2022|A.8.9,ITSG-33|CM-6b.,LEVEL|2A,NESA|T3.2.1,Rule-ID|SV-257788r1044838_rule,STIG-ID|RHEL-09-212015,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.3,Vuln-ID|V-257788"
      see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/22008"
      cmd         : "(/sbin/grubby --info=ALL | /bin/grep args | /bin/grep 'systemd.confirm_spawn') 2>&1 | /bin/awk '{print} END {if (NR == 0) print \"pass\" ; else print \"fail\"}'"
      expect      : "^pass$"
    </custom_item>

