        <report type:"PASSED">
          description : "1.188 RHEL-09-253040"
          info        : "RHEL 9 must prevent IPv4 Internet Control Message Protocol (ICMP) redirect messages from being accepted.

GROUP ID: V-257963
RULE ID: SV-257963r991589

ICMP redirect messages are used by routers to inform hosts that a more direct route exists for a particular destination. These messages modify the host's route table and are unauthenticated. An illicit ICMP redirect message could result in a man-in-the-middle attack.

This feature of the IPv4 protocol has few legitimate uses. It must be disabled unless absolutely required."
          solution    : "Configure RHEL 9 to prevent IPv4 ICMP redirect messages from being accepted.

Add or edit the following line in a single system configuration file, in the \"/etc/sysctl.d/\" directory:

net.ipv4.conf.default.accept_redirects = 0

Load settings from all system configuration files with the following command:

$ sudo sysctl --system"
