    <custom_item>
      type        : CMD_EXEC
      description : "1.218 RHEL-09-255080"
      info        : "RHEL 9 must not allow a noncertificate trusted host SSH logon to the system.

GROUP ID: V-257992
RULE ID: SV-257992r1045047

SSH trust relationships mean a compromise on one host can allow an attacker to move trivially to other hosts."
      solution    : "To configure RHEL 9 to not allow a noncertificate trusted host SSH logon to the system, add or modify the following line in \"/etc/ssh/sshd_config\" or in a file in \"/etc/ssh/sshd_config.d\".

HostbasedAuthentication no

Restart the SSH daemon for the settings to take effect:

$ sudo systemctl restart sshd.service"
      reference   : "800-171|3.4.2,800-171r3|03.04.02a.,800-53|CM-6b.,800-53r5|CM-6b.,CAT|II,CCI|CCI-000366,CN-L3|8.1.10.6(d),CSF|PR.IP-1,CSF2.0|DE.CM-09,CSF2.0|PR.PS-01,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ISO-27001-2022|A.8.9,ITSG-33|CM-6b.,LEVEL|2A,NESA|T3.2.1,Rule-ID|SV-257992r1045047_rule,STIG-ID|RHEL-09-255080,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.3,Vuln-ID|V-257992"
      see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/22008"
      cmd         : "/sbin/sshd -T | /bin/grep -i HostbasedAuthentication"
      expect      : "(?i)[\\s]*HostbasedAuthentication[\\s]+\"?no\"?[\\s]*$"
    </custom_item>

