    <if>
      <condition auto:"FAILED" type:"AND">
        <custom_item>
          type            : FILE_CONTENT_CHECK
          description     : "install usb-storage /bin/false"
          file            : "/etc/modprobe.d/* /etc/modprobe.conf"
          regex           : "^[\\s]*install[\\s]+usb-storage"
          expect          : "^[\\s]*install[\\s]+usb-storage[\\s]+/bin/false[\\s]*$"
          required        : NO
          min_occurrences : "1"
        </custom_item>

        <custom_item>
          type            : FILE_CONTENT_CHECK
          description     : "blacklist usb-storage"
          file            : "/etc/modprobe.d/* /etc/modprobe.conf"
          regex           : "^[\\s]*blacklist[\\s]+usb-storage"
          expect          : "^[\\s]*blacklist[\\s]+usb-storage[\\s]*$"
          required        : NO
          min_occurrences : "1"
        </custom_item>
      </condition>

      <then>
        <report type:"PASSED">
          description : "1.259 RHEL-09-291010"
          info        : "RHEL 9 must be configured to disable USB mass storage.

GROUP ID: V-258034
RULE ID: SV-258034r1051267

USB mass storage permits easy introduction of unknown devices, thereby facilitating malicious activity.

Satisfies: SRG-OS-000114-GPOS-00059, SRG-OS-000378-GPOS-00163, SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227"
          solution    : "To configure the system to prevent the usb-storage kernel module from being loaded, add the following lines to the file \"/etc/modprobe.d/usb-storage.conf\" (or create \"usb-storage.conf\" if it does not exist):

install usb-storage /bin/false
blacklist usb-storage"
