      see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/22008"
      file        : "/etc/sudoers /etc/sudoers.d/*"
      regex       : "^[^#]*!authenticate"
      expect      : "^[^#]*!authenticate"
    </custom_item>

    <custom_item>
      type        : FILE_CONTENT_CHECK_NOT
      description : "1.308 RHEL-09-432030"
      info        : "RHEL 9 must restrict privilege elevation to authorized personnel.

GROUP ID: V-258087
RULE ID: SV-258087r1045177

If the \"sudoers\" file is not configured correctly, any user defined on the system can initiate privileged actions on the target system."
      solution    : "Remove the following entries from the /etc/sudoers file or configuration file under /etc/sudoers.d/:

ALL ALL=(ALL) ALL
ALL ALL=(ALL:ALL) ALL"
      reference   : "800-171|3.4.2,800-171r3|03.04.02a.,800-53|CM-6b.,800-53r5|CM-6b.,CAT|II,CCI|CCI-000366,CN-L3|8.1.10.6(d),CSF|PR.IP-1,CSF2.0|DE.CM-09,CSF2.0|PR.PS-01,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ISO-27001-2022|A.8.9,ITSG-33|CM-6b.,LEVEL|2A,NESA|T3.2.1,Rule-ID|SV-258087r1045177_rule,STIG-ID|RHEL-09-432030,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.3,Vuln-ID|V-258087"
      see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/22008"
      file        : "/etc/sudoers /etc/sudoers.d/*"
      regex       : "^[\\s]*ALL[\\s]+"
      expect      : "^[\\s]*ALL[\\s]+ALL=\\(ALL(:ALL)?\\)[\\s]+ALL"
    </custom_item>

    <custom_item>
      type        : FILE_CONTENT_CHECK
      description : "1.309 RHEL-09-432035"
      info        : "RHEL 9 must restrict the use of the \"su\" command.

GROUP ID: V-258088
RULE ID: SV-258088r1050789

The \"su\" program allows to run commands with a substitute user and group ID. It is commonly used to run commands as the root user. Limiting access to such commands is considered a good security practice.

Satisfies: SRG-OS-000373-GPOS-00156, SRG-OS-000312-GPOS-00123"
      solution    : "Configure RHEL 9 to require users to be in the \"wheel\" group to run \"su\" command.

In file \"/etc/pam.d/su\", uncomment the following line:

\"#auth required pam_wheel.so use_uid\"

$ sed '/^[[:space:]]*#[[:space:]]*auth[[:space:]]\\+required[[:space:]]\\+pam_wheel\\.so[[:space:]]\\+use_uid$/s/^[[:space:]]*#//' -i /etc/pam.d/su

If necessary, create a \"wheel\" group and add administrative users to the group."
      reference   : "800-171|3.1.1,800-171r3|03.01.02,800-171r3|03.05.01b.,800-53|AC-3(4),800-53|IA-11,800-53r5|AC-3(4),800-53r5|SC-11b.,CAT|II,CCI|CCI-002038,CCI|CCI-002165,CCI|CCI-004895,CN-L3|8.1.4.2(f),CN-L3|8.1.4.11(b),CN-L3|8.1.10.2(c),CN-L3|8.5.3.1,CN-L3|8.5.4.1(a),CSF|PR.AC-1,CSF|PR.AC-4,CSF|PR.PT-3,CSF2.0|PR.AA-01,CSF2.0|PR.AA-03,CSF2.0|PR.AA-05,CSF2.0|PR.DS-10,CSF2.0|PR.IR-01,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),HIPAA|164.312(a)(1),HIPAA|164.312(d),ISO-27001-2022|A.5.15,ISO-27001-2022|A.5.33,ISO-27001-2022|A.8.3,ISO-27001-2022|A.8.18,ISO-27001-2022|A.8.20,ISO/IEC-27001|A.9.4.1,ISO/IEC-27001|A.9.4.5,ITSG-33|AC-3(4),LEVEL|2A,NESA|T4.2.1,NESA|T5.4.4,NESA|T5.4.5,NESA|T5.5.4,NESA|T5.6.1,NESA|T7.5.2,NESA|T7.5.3,NIAv2|AM3,NIAv2|SS29,QCSC-v1|3.2,QCSC-v1|5.2.2,QCSC-v1|13.2,Rule-ID|SV-258088r1050789_rule,STIG-ID|RHEL-09-432035,TBA-FIISB|31.1,Vuln-ID|V-258088"
      see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/22008"
      file        : "/etc/pam.d/su"
      regex       : "^[\\s]*auth[\\s]+required[\\s]+pam_wheel\\.so[\\s]+(?=[^#]*\\buse_uid\\b)[^#]*"
      expect      : "^[\\s]*auth[\\s]+required[\\s]+pam_wheel\\.so[\\s]+(?=[^#]*\\buse_uid\\b)[^#]*"
    </custom_item>

    <if>
      <condition auto:"FAILED" type:"AND">
        <custom_item>
          type            : FILE_CONTENT_CHECK
          description     : "sctp /bin/false"
          file            : "/etc/modprobe.d/* /etc/modprobe.conf"
