      see_also        : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/22008"
      file            : "/etc/security/limits.conf /etc/security/limits.d/*.conf"
      regex           : "^[^#]*core[\\s]+"
      expect          : "^[^#]*core[\\s]+0[\\s]*$"
      file_required   : NO
      min_occurrences : "1"
      string_required : NO
    </custom_item>

    <custom_item>
      type        : FILE_CONTENT_CHECK
      description : "1.380 RHEL-09-653075"
      info        : "RHEL 9 audit system must audit local events.

GROUP ID: V-258164
RULE ID: SV-258164r1045301

Without establishing what type of events occurred, the source of events, where events occurred, and the outcome of events, it would be difficult to establish, correlate, and investigate the events leading up to an outage or attack.

If option \"local_events\" isn't set to \"yes\" only events from network will be aggregated.

Satisfies: SRG-OS-000062-GPOS-00031, SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227"
      solution    : "Configure RHEL 9 to generate audit records for local events by adding or updating the following line in \"/etc/audit/auditd.conf\":

local_events = yes

The audit daemon must be restarted for the changes to take effect."
