    <custom_item>
      type        : FILE_CONTENT_CHECK
      description : "1.384 RHEL-09-653095"
      info        : "RHEL 9 must periodically flush audit records to disk to prevent the loss of audit records.

GROUP ID: V-258168
RULE ID: SV-258168r958428

If option \"freq\" is not set to a value that requires audit records being written to disk after a threshold number is reached, then audit records may be lost."
      solution    : "Configure RHEL 9 to flush audit to disk by adding or updating the following rule in \"/etc/audit/auditd.conf\":

freq = 100

The audit daemon must be restarted for the changes to take effect."
      reference   : "800-171|3.3.1,800-171r3|03.03.05,800-53|AU-6(4),800-53r5|AU-6(4),CAT|II,CCI|CCI-000154,CN-L3|7.1.3.3(d),CSF|DE.AE-2,CSF|DE.AE-3,CSF|DE.DP-4,CSF|PR.PT-1,CSF|RS.AN-1,CSF|RS.CO-2,CSF2.0|DE.AE-02,CSF2.0|DE.AE-03,CSF2.0|PR.PS-04,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),HIPAA|164.312(b),ISO-27001-2022|A.5.25,ISO-27001-2022|A.6.8,ISO-27001-2022|A.8.15,ITSG-33|AU-6(4),LEVEL|2A,NESA|M5.2.5,QCSC-v1|5.2.3,QCSC-v1|8.2.1,QCSC-v1|10.2.1,QCSC-v1|11.2,QCSC-v1|13.2,Rule-ID|SV-258168r958428_rule,STIG-ID|RHEL-09-653095,SWIFT-CSCv1|6.4,Vuln-ID|V-258168"
      see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/22008"
      file        : "/etc/audit/auditd.conf"
      regex       : "(?i)^[\\s]*freq[\\s]*=[\\s]*"
      expect      : "(?i)^[\\s]*freq[\\s]*=[\\s]*(?:[1-9]|[1-9][0-9]|100)[\\s]*$"
    </custom_item>

    <custom_item>
      type        : FILE_CONTENT_CHECK
      description : "1.385 RHEL-09-653100"
      info        : "RHEL 9 must produce audit records containing information to establish the identity of any individual or process associated with the event.

GROUP ID: V-258169
RULE ID: SV-258169r991556

Without establishing what type of events occurred, the source of events, where events occurred, and the outcome of events, it would be difficult to establish, correlate, and investigate the events leading up to an outage or attack.

Audit record content that may be necessary to satisfy this requirement includes, for example, time stamps, source and destination addresses, user/process identifiers, event descriptions, success/fail indications, filenames involved, and access control or flow control rules invoked.

Enriched logging aids in making sense of who, what, and when events occur on a system. Without this, determining root cause of an event will be much more difficult.

Satisfies: SRG-OS-000255-GPOS-00096, SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227"
      solution    : "Edit the /etc/audit/auditd.conf file and add or update the \"log_format\" option:

log_format = ENRICHED

The audit daemon must be restarted for changes to take effect."
      reference   : "800-171|3.3.1,800-171|3.3.2,800-171|3.4.2,800-171r3|03.03.02a.,800-171r3|03.04.02a.,800-53|AU-3,800-53|CM-6b.,800-53r5|AU-3f.,800-53r5|CM-6b.,CAT|II,CCI|CCI-000366,CCI|CCI-001487,CN-L3|7.1.2.3(a),CN-L3|7.1.2.3(b),CN-L3|7.1.3.3(a),CN-L3|8.1.4.3(b),CN-L3|8.1.10.6(d),CSF|PR.IP-1,CSF|PR.PT-1,CSF2.0|DE.CM-09,CSF2.0|PR.PS-01,CSF2.0|PR.PS-04,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),HIPAA|164.312(b),ISO-27001-2022|A.5.28,ISO-27001-2022|A.8.9,ISO-27001-2022|A.8.15,ITSG-33|AU-3,ITSG-33|CM-6b.,LEVEL|2A,NESA|T3.2.1,NESA|T3.6.2,NIAv2|AM34a,NIAv2|AM34b,NIAv2|AM34c,NIAv2|AM34d,NIAv2|AM34e,NIAv2|AM34f,NIAv2|AM34g,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|10.3,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|10.3.1,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|10.3.2,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|10.3.3,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|10.3.4,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|10.3.5,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|10.3.6,PCI-DSSv4.0|10.2.2,QCSC-v1|8.2.1,QCSC-v1|13.2,Rule-ID|SV-258169r991556_rule,STIG-ID|RHEL-09-653100,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.3,SWIFT-CSCv1|6.4,Vuln-ID|V-258169"
      see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/22008"
      file        : "/etc/audit/auditd.conf"
      regex       : "(?i)^[\\s]*log_format[\\s]*=[\\s]*"
      expect      : "(?i)^[\\s]*log_format[\\s]*=[\\s]*ENRICHED[\\s]*$"
