      see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/22008"
      file        : "/etc/pam.d/password-auth"
      regex       : "^[\\s]*password([^#\\n\\r]+)pam_unix\\.so"
      expect      : "^[\\s]*password([^#\\n\\r]+)pam_unix\\.so([^#\\n\\r]+)(?i)@PASSWORD_ENCRYPTION@(?-i)"
    </custom_item>

    <custom_item>
      type        : CMD_EXEC
      description : "1.451 RHEL-09-672025"
      info        : "RHEL 9 must use mechanisms meeting the requirements of applicable federal laws, executive orders, directives, policies, regulations, standards, and guidance for authentication to a cryptographic module.

GROUP ID: V-258237RULE ID: SV-258237r1051256

Overriding the system crypto policy makes the behavior of Kerberos violate expectations and makes system configuration more fragmented."
      solution    : "Configure Kerberos to use system cryptographic policy.

Create a symlink pointing to system crypto policy in the Kerberos configuration using the following command:

$ sudo ln -s /etc/crypto-policies/back-ends/krb5.config /usr/share/crypto-policies/FIPS/krb5.txt"
